.TH URMA-BROWSER 1 urma-browser\-VERSION
.SH NAME
urma-browser \- experimental URMA browser based on surf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B urma-browser
.RB [-bBdDfFgGiIkKmMnNpPsStTvwxX]
.RB [-a\ cookiepolicies]
.RB [-c\ cookiefile]
.RB [-C\ stylefile]
.RB [-e\ xid]
.RB [-r\ scriptfile]
.RB [-u\ useragent]
.RB [-z\ zoomlevel]
.RB [URI]
.SH DESCRIPTION
URMA Browser is an experimental surf-derived browser using WebKitGTK.
It provides an inline address bar, native tabs, publication details and
registry settings. The separate
.B urma
CLI supplies verified URMA packages and name resolution; it is not bundled.
The installed executable and extension directory use the
.B urma-browser
namespace. Source filenames and inherited profile paths retain surf names.
.PP
With no URI, the local about:blank start page offers an address action, New tab,
Settings and Shortcuts. Its embedded presentation makes no CLI or network request.
Page-created blank windows retain their own content.
.SH URMA ADDRESSES
Accepted forms are
.BR urma://ROOT_TXID.NET/ ,
.BR urma://NAME.NET/
and
.BR urma://GENESIS.NAME.NET/ .
Networks are ltc, tltc, tbtc and btc; Bitcoin mainnet is not enabled by the
reference CLI. The rbtc test form requires URMA_SURF_REGTEST=1.
No name registry is activated by default. Names require a local index
created and updated explicitly with
.BR "urma names scan" .
Selecting a registry does not scan it.
.PP
An explicit registry differing from the tab's effective choice offers Temporary,
Global or Cancel. Temporary commits one network-registry pair to the tab only
after successful navigation; another network uses its global registry.
Global resolves the selected registry and saves its persistent slot before
loading; resolve or save failure refuses the choice without fallback.
Cancel and failed temporary navigation retain the previous document/context.
The visible Use global action clears that tab's temporary scope, stops pending
navigation and prevents history from restoring old temporary choices.
Back/Forward otherwise restore committed scope and binding. Relative links and
reload retain publication context. Derived tabs receive an independent scope
copy and keep the copied name binding for the same publication; blank tabs use
global slots. Settings changes persistent global slots.
.PP
Documents render at a publication origin identified by network and root TXID.
The CLI re-verifies retained proofs and the package; the browser checks resource
hashes and lengths against the declared set. Undeclared paths and
cross-publication initiators are refused. URMA page network traffic is blocked;
the separate CLI fetch operation can still contact its configured source.
Offline checks establish retained authorship and content, not current chain
inclusion, finality or an independently proven network. The verified badge
does not imply a fresh chain scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a cookiepolicies
Define the order of
.I cookie policies\fR.
The default is "@Aa" but could be
redefined in the
.IR config.h ,
with "A" meaning to
accept all cookies, "a" to deny all cookies and "@", which tells surf to
accept no third party cookies.
.TP
.B \-b
Disable Scrollbars.
.TP
.B \-B
Enable Scrollbars.
.TP
.B \-c cookiefile
Specify the
.I cookiefile
to use.
.TP
.B \-C stylefile
Specify the user
.IR stylefile .
This does disable the site-specific styles.
.TP
.B \-d
Disable the disk cache.
.TP
.B \-D
Enable the disk cache.
.TP
.B \-e xid
Reparents to window specified by
.IR xid .
.TP
.B \-f
Start surf in windowed mode (not fullscreen).
.TP
.B \-F
Start surf in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-g
Disable giving the geolocation to websites.
.TP
.B \-G
Enable giving the geolocation to websites.
.TP
.B \-i
Disable Images.
.TP
.B \-I
Enable Images.
.TP
.B \-k
Disable kiosk mode (enable key strokes and right click).
.TP
.B \-K
Enable kiosk mode (disable key strokes and right click).
.TP
.B \-m
Disable application of user style sheets.
.TP
.B \-M
Enable application of user style sheets.
.TP
.B \-n
Disable the Web Inspector (Developer Tools).
.TP
.B \-N
Enable the Web Inspector (Developer Tools).
.TP
.B \-r scriptfile
Specify the user
.IR scriptfile .
.TP
.B \-s
Disable Javascript.
.TP
.B \-S
Enable Javascript.
.TP
.B \-t
Disable strict TLS check.
.TP
.B \-T
Enable strict TLS check.
.TP
.B \-u useragent
Specify the
.I useragent
which surf should use.
.TP
.B \-v
Prints version information, then exits.
.TP
.B \-w
Prints xid to standard output. This can be used to script the browser in for
example
.BR xdotool(1) .
.TP
.B -x
Disable custom certificates.
.TP
.B -X
Enable custom certificates.
.TP
.B \-z zoomlevel
Specify the
.I zoomlevel
which surf should use.
.SH USAGE
Keyboard navigation uses the inline address and find bars; dmenu is not required.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-l or F6
Focus and select the address.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-t / Ctrl\-w
Open / close a tab. Closing the last tab closes its window.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Tab / Ctrl\-Shift\-Tab
Select the next / previous tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-1 through Ctrl\-8 / Ctrl\-9
Select a numbered tab / the last tab.
.TP
.B Alt\-Left or Ctrl\-[ / Alt\-Right or Ctrl\-]
Back / forward.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-f or Ctrl\-/
Find in page. Enter selects the next match, Shift\-Enter the previous;
Escape closes the find bar.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-n / Ctrl\-Shift\-n
Next / previous search match.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-r or F5
Reload.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-r or Ctrl\-F5
Reload while bypassing the page cache.
.TP
.B Escape or Ctrl\-c
Stop loading.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-+ or Ctrl\-= / Ctrl\--
Zoom in / out. Ctrl and the scroll wheel also zoom.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-0
Reset zoom to 100 percent.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-,
Open settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-d
Show publication details.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-y / Ctrl\-Shift\-u
Copy link / copy link with the registry.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-y / Ctrl\-p
Copy the page address / open selected text as an address.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-b
Show or hide the address bar.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-p
Print.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-o
Open the web inspector when enabled.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-?
Show the complete shortcut sheet.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.SH INDICATORS OF OPERATION
The optional upstream toggle indicators are disabled by default.
When ShowIndicators is enabled in configuration, they precede the site title.
For all indicators, unless otherwise specified, a lower case letter means disabled and an upper case letter means enabled.
.TP
.B A
all cookies accepted
.TP
.B a
no cookies accepted
.TP
.B @
all except third-party cookies accepted
.TP
.B c C
caret browsing
.TP
.B g G
geolocation
.TP
.B d D
disk cache
.TP
.B i I
images
.TP
.B s S
scripts
.TP
.B m M
styles
.TP
.B x X
custom certificates
.TP
.B t T
strict TLS
.SH INDICATORS OF WEB PAGE
The second part of the indicators specifies modes of the web page itself.
.SS First character: encryption
.TP
.B -
unencrypted
.TP
.B T
encrypted (TLS)
.TP
.B U
attempted encryption but failed
.SS Second character: proxying
.TP
.B -
no proxy
.TP
.B P
using proxy
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B URMA_BIN
CLI executable; defaults to urma on PATH.
.TP
.B URMA_WEB_STORE
Verified store directory; defaults to XDG_DATA_HOME/urma/web-store or
~/.local/share/urma/web-store.
.TP
.B URMA_NAMES_DIR
Names index directory; defaults to XDG_DATA_HOME/urma/names or
~/.local/share/urma/names. Indexes are stored as CHAIN/GENESIS.json.
.TP
.B URMA_CONFIG
Inherited CLI configuration path.
.TP
.B URMA_RPC_URL and URMA_NODE_AUTH_FILE
Inherited CLI local node configuration and authentication cookie-file path.
.TP
.B URMA_SURF_REGTEST
Set to 1 for the isolated regtest address form.
.TP
.B SURF_USERAGENT
Inherited user agent override.
.TP
.B http_proxy
Inherited ordinary browser proxy. URMA pages use their isolated network context.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.surf/urma-registries.ini
Persistent active registry slots in the [active] group, keyed by network suffix.
There is no automatic active registry.
.TP
.B ~/.surf/
Inherited browser cookies, cache, user styles and certificates.
Native tabs share a WebKit profile.
.TP
.B PREFIX/share/doc/urma-browser/
Installed README, MIT/X copyright and license, complete OFL notice and asset
provenance. The separate CLI and local user state are not part of this package.
.SH SIGNALS
The browser reloads the current page on
.BR SIGHUP .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xprop(1),
.BR xdotool(1)
.PP
The standalone source README and tests/README.md describe build dependencies,
the exact CLI integration revision and the separate sanitizer, GUI and
authentic-store gates. Ordinary non-URMA helper actions may need st, curl,
xdg-open or mpv as configured.
.SH STATUS
Version VERSION is an experimental source preparation, not a stable release.
See NOTICES.md for upstream and asset provenance, including the unresolved
mark redistribution permission before public distribution.
